section: compiler
synopsis: Build the unit state from the units named by id when ``-hide-all-packages`` is set.
description:
  With ``-hide-all-packages`` and unit ids on every package flag, which is
  how Cabal and environment files drive GHC, the compiler builds its unit
  state from the units named and their dependencies only. A unit store is
  not enumerated; package databases are still read, but units outside that
  closure are not validated, do not appear in ``--show-packages`` and are
  not mentioned as hidden when a module is not found. The new
  ``-trust-id ⟨unit-id⟩`` and ``-distrust-id ⟨unit-id⟩`` flags are the
  by-id forms of ``-trust`` and ``-distrust``. Nothing changes for command
  lines that name a package by name.
